Dear all,

I am trying to fit a simple linear growth model to categorical data. I have observed the log of the wage over seven different time points (1980 to 1987). I would like to compare the results obtained  using the underlying variable approach, with estimation performed using uni and bivariate information (UBN, estimator="WLSMV") as well as full information (UMN, estimator="FML").

I do not have problem in getting the UBN solution, whereas it is almost impossible to get the UMN solution based on the estimator FML. I always end up with the error message

Error in sadmvn(lower, upper, mean = MEAN, varcov = Sigma.hat, maxpts = 10000 *  :
  lower>upper integration limits

I also considered a smaller number of time points, since if I have correctly understood full information maximum likelihood under the underlying variable approach is possibile for at maximum a six-dimensional integral.

Below the syntax I wrote for both UBN and UMN:

model.0.cat <http://model.0.cat><-'
#measurement model
alpha=~1*lnwg_cat_80+1*lnwg_cat_81+1*lnwg_cat_82+1*lnwg_cat_83+1*lnwg_cat_84+1*lnwg_cat_85+1*lnwg_cat_86+1*lnwg_cat_87
beta=~0*lnwg_cat_80+1*lnwg_cat_81+2*lnwg_cat_82+3*lnwg_cat_83+4*lnwg_cat_84+5*lnwg_cat_85+6*lnwg_cat_86+7*lnwg_cat_87

lnwg_cat_80|0*t1+1*t2+tau3*t3
lnwg_cat_81|0*t1+1*t2+tau3*t3
lnwg_cat_82|0*t1+1*t2+tau3*t3
lnwg_cat_83|0*t1+1*t2+tau3*t3
lnwg_cat_84|0*t1+1*t2+tau3*t3
lnwg_cat_85|0*t1+1*t2+tau3*t3
lnwg_cat_86|0*t1+1*t2+tau3*t3
lnwg_cat_87|0*t1+1*t2+tau3*t3

#structural model
alpha~1
beta~1
alpha~~beta
alpha~~alpha
beta~~beta
'
#UBN
fit.0.cat <http://fit.0.cat><-cfa(model.0.cat <http://model.0.cat>,data=lnwg_cat,estimator="WLSMVS",parameterization="theta")
summary(fit.0.cat <http://fit.0.cat>, fit.measure=TRUE)

model.1.cat <http://model.1.cat><-'
#measurement model
alpha=~1*lnwg_cat_80+1*lnwg_cat_81+1*lnwg_cat_82+1*lnwg_cat_83+1*lnwg_cat_84+1*lnwg_cat_85
beta=~0*lnwg_cat_80+1*lnwg_cat_81+2*lnwg_cat_82+3*lnwg_cat_83+4*lnwg_cat_84+5*lnwg_cat_85

lnwg_cat_80|0*t1+1*t2+tau3*t3
lnwg_cat_81|0*t1+1*t2+tau3*t3
lnwg_cat_82|0*t1+1*t2+tau3*t3
lnwg_cat_83|0*t1+1*t2+tau3*t3
lnwg_cat_84|0*t1+1*t2+tau3*t3
lnwg_cat_85|0*t1+1*t2+tau3*t3

#structural model
alpha~1
beta~1
alpha~~beta
alpha~~alpha
beta~~beta
'
#UMN
fit.1.cat <http://fit.1.cat><-cfa(model.1.cat <http://model.1.cat>,data=lnwg_cat,estimator="FML",parameterization="theta")
summary(fit.1.cat <http://fit.1.cat>, fit.measure=TRUE)

Thank you!
Silvia

